6. Build classical soliton/monopole claims from a fully specified action,
   boundary conditions and topological charge. Build quantum BPS claims only
   from the sibling's exact algebra/central-charge supplier and a defined
   protected Hilbert-space index.
7. Reuse the finite-field Hall/HN theorem and the CY3 bridge contract as
   mathematical/algebraic context. Any physical DT/BPS identity, all-regime
   chamber spectrum, refined index, or spectral-network reconstruction needs
   its own model-specific proof or a dated, source-reviewed open-problem
   record.

