+---
+id: def-abbv-equivariant-integration-conventions
+kind: definition
+title: "Borel Equivariant Integration Conventions for the ABBV Formula"
+status: draft
+origin: pipeline
+domain: mathematics
+library: mathematics
+dependency_level: 1
+deps:
+  - def-torus-equivariant-cohomology-cartan-model
+dependency_roles:
+  def-torus-equivariant-cohomology-cartan-model: mathematical-premise
+provenance:
+  statement: ai-altered
+  proof: not-applicable
+sources:
+  scraped: []
+  references:
+    - title: "Michael F. Atiyah and Raoul Bott, The Moment Map and Equivariant Cohomology"
+      url: "https://www.math.stonybrook.edu/~mmovshev/MAT570Spring2008/BOOKS/atiyahbott_moment.pdf"
+    - title: "Matvei Libine, Lecture Notes on Equivariant Cohomology"
+      url: "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0709.3615"
+verification:
+  precheck: pending
+---
+
+## Definition
+
+Let $T$ be a compact torus of rank $r$, with character lattice $X^*(T)=\operatorname{Hom}(T,S^1)$. For a smooth $T$-manifold $X$, choose a contractible free $T$-space $ET$, write $BT=ET/T$, and define the rational Borel equivariant cohomology by $H_T^*(X;\mathbb Q)=H^*(ET\times_T X;\mathbb Q)$. Its coefficient ring is $R=H^*(BT;\mathbb Q)\cong\operatorname{Sym}(X^*(T)\otimes\mathbb Q)$, with characters in degree $2$. For $\chi\in X^*(T)$, let $B\chi:BT\to BS^1=\mathbb{CP}^{\infty}$ be induced by $\chi$ and set $u_\chi=(B\chi)^*h$, where $h\in H^2(\mathbb{CP}^{\infty};\mathbb Q)$ restricts to the positive generator on the complex-oriented $\mathbb{CP}^1$. Thus $u_\chi\ne0$ exactly when $\chi$ is nontrivial. Let $S\subset R$ be the multiplicative set generated by all such nonzero $u_\chi$, including $1$; write $S^{-1}H_T^*(X;\mathbb Q)$ and $S^{-1}R$ for the corresponding localizations.
+
+If $X$ is a compact oriented smooth $T$-manifold without boundary of dimension $n$ and the action preserves its orientation, the Borel projection $\pi_X:ET\times_T X\to BT$ has compact oriented $n$-dimensional fibers. Define equivariant integration $\int_X\alpha=(\pi_X)_!\alpha$, the cohomological pushforward along those fibers; it lowers degree by $n$ and has values in $R$. For an oriented $T$-equivariant vector bundle $E\to X$ whose Borel-associated bundle has a normalized Thom class, define its equivariant Euler class $e_T(E)$ as the pullback of that Thom class by the zero section. The Thom class is normalized to restrict on each oriented fiber pair $(D^c,S^{c-1})$ to the positive generator of $H^c(D^c,S^{c-1};\mathbb Q)$. For a complex $T$-representation line of character $\chi$, this convention gives Euler class $u_\chi$. For a fixed component $F$ of a $T$-action on $M$, the orientation convention is $o(TM|_F)=o(TF)\wedge o(\nu_F)$, where $\nu_F$ is its chosen equivariantly oriented normal bundle. This is the Borel convention; no identification with a Cartan, Chow, or quotient-stack cohomology model is assumed here.
+
+## Definition references
+
+[[def-torus-equivariant-cohomology-cartan-model]]
+
+[Atiyah and Bott, §2, equations (2.1)–(2.9)](https://www.math.stonybrook.edu/~mmovshev/MAT570Spring2008/BOOKS/atiyahbott_moment.pdf)
+
+[Libine, §2.1, Definition 3, and §5.3](https://arxiv.org/pdf/0709.3615)
