lem-abbv-equivariant-thom-gysin-identities
zero step 1.3: all Gysin constructions are linear, so beta=0 gives zero on both sides.
degenerate step 2.1: if c=0, the fiber Thom class is 1 and the self-intersection identity reduces to the identity map.
nonempty-choice step 1.1: one Haar average constructs a single invariant metric; compactness gives a tubular neighborhood, and the cellular proof uses no arbitrary-index choice.

lem-abbv-fixed-component-euler-invertibility
zero step 2.2: the nilpotent remainder vanishes when it is zero, leaving the unit f_j^{-1}.
degenerate step 2.2: rank-zero normal bundle has empty weight product 1 and Euler class 1.
nonempty-choice step 1.3: the weight set is finite, so a Lie-algebra element outside its finitely many proper kernels exists; if there are no weights, no choice is needed.

thm-atiyah-bott-berline-vergne-integration-formula
