+# Batch 9 — Step 1 authoring evidence
+
+Run: `advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23`  
+Batch: 9 (`beta`, `quantum-field-theory-mathematics`)
+
+## Scope, design, and dependency levels
+
+The complete assigned design section in `research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md` matches the relevant `research/plan-spec.json` page records: A page `qftx-abbv-integration`, B page `qftx-abbv-integration-examples`, order 965, title, category `quantum-field-theory-mathematics`, mathematics library, and A-page prerequisite `qftx-borel-localization`. The design covers compact oriented finite-dimensional fixed-component pushforward with normal Euler denominators and isolated-fixed-point specialization. It excludes arbitrary noncompact instanton spaces and infinite-dimensional field spaces. The empty plan item arrays are scaffolding placeholders. No plan/design conflict was found, and shared plans and proposed inventories were not edited.
+
+The run dependency-level record gives batch 8 level 1 (requiring batch 7) and batch 9 level 2 (requiring batch 8). The authored item levels are 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, and 7: local Borel convention → local Gysin lemma → local Euler-invertibility lemma → ABBV theorem → two examples. The current batch-8 manifest now correctly places `lem-qftx-borel-base-is-paracompact-of-cw-type` at level 2, after `lem-qftx-compact-manifold-cohomology-positive-ideal-nilpotent` at level 1. Thus the assigned Gysin level 4 remains consistent; rerun the scoped level checker after all edits.
+
+## Live prerequisite inspection and current gaps
+
+The current batch-7 manifest contains `def-torus-equivariant-cohomology-cartan-model` on `qftx-equivariant-cohomology` at item level 2. I reread its Borel definition and the transitive coefficient lemma `lem-torus-classifying-space-cohomology`: the selected product Milnor model, real Borel quotient, period-one basis, and tautological-Euler normalization match the local convention. `loadStep1Record`/`step1Decision` now return `closed: true` for both the Borel definition (row SHA256 `5487bc1bcee36dafba1b3e4747874ed8427cefc586a5a1f8ec92687e20924551`, 2026-10-23T08:29:48.868Z) and coefficient lemma (row SHA256 `e218284e79262081b742030f2623af4efbed620a2bca954f0406b323448dd6b5`, 2026-10-23T08:29:40.656Z). This supersedes the earlier checkpoint that called these records stale. The local convention is ready after its own scoped checks and new record.
+
+The file `items/thm-borel-localization-for-compact-torus-actions.md` is present in the batch-8 manifest, and its entire current statement and proof have been inspected. Its real-coefficient statement matches the local use: compact finite-dimensional Hausdorff second-countable smooth manifold without boundary; product right Milnor Borel model; multiplicative set generated by nontrivial-character first Chern classes; localized fixed-locus restriction isomorphism. The local definition explicitly identifies those first Chern classes with the Euler classes `u_chi`, so the localized sets agree. The current proof now cites the required `lem-qftx-borel-base-is-paracompact-of-cw-type` and the Thom/numerability inputs in [F6], and the theorem's direct dependencies include them. Nevertheless, `step1Decision` returns `Readiness record missing` for the localization theorem, the base-property lemma, and `def-qftx-character-localization`; these are current readiness blockers, not inferences from `draft` status or absent independent approval. The real character-localization item's [F1] still says `def-torus-equivariant-cohomology-cartan-model` lacks a current Step 1 record, although that batch-7 record is now closed. This stale evidence note is an owner escalation; it was not repaired here.
+
+The assigned A-page `requires` edge to `qftx-borel-localization` is verified at the page-interface level: the batch-8 page file and current manifest both contain the Borel theorem and helper inventory. This does not close the unresolved Step 1 readiness of the item suppliers. The main theorem consumes the exact current Borel theorem statement conditionally and is escalated until those item-level records are current.
+
+## Source retrieval and inspected passages
+
+Three full-text treatments were inspected. All three full PDFs are fetch-verified in `batch-9.coverage.json`; no source was dropped. Clay's PDF required two 90-second recovery attempts before the full body succeeded. The three searches, all attempts, SHA-256 prefixes, byte counts, page counts, timestamps, item mappings, and per-item dispositions are preserved in coverage evidence.
+
+- Michael F. Atiyah and Raoul Bott, “The Moment Map and Equivariant Cohomology,” complete 28-page PDF: <https://www.math.stonybrook.edu/~mmovshev/MAT570Spring2008/BOOKS/atiyahbott_moment.pdf>. Inspected §2, PDF pp. 2–4, equations (2.1)–(2.9), and §3, PDF pp. 7–9, Theorem 3.5 through equations (3.7)–(3.8): Borel construction, support/localization, Thom-Gysin self-intersection, normal-weight Euler inversion, and pushforward formula. Its introduction explicitly says the proof does not directly apply in infinite dimensions.
+- Matvei Libine, “Lecture Notes on Equivariant Cohomology,” complete 72-page graduate lecture notes: <https://arxiv.org/pdf/0709.3615>. Inspected §2.1 Definition 3, PDF pp. 1–2; §5.3 Euler classes, pp. 14–16; and §7.7, Theorems 69–71, pp. 41–44, including the fixed-component pushforward and localized inverse. The notes follow Atiyah–Bott, Berline–Vergne, and Guillemin–Sternberg; they are an independently authored full exposition. Their differential-form formula in §§7.1–7.3 includes explicit `(2π)` factors; the authored Borel Thom class integrates to 1 on each oriented fiber, so those factors are not imported into the cohomological convention.
+- Kentaro Hori et al., *Mirror Symmetry*, complete 952-page Clay Mathematics Monographs volume: <https://www.claymath.org/library/monographs/cmim-1.pdf>. Inspected Chapter 4 §4.3, printed pp. 62–64 / PDF pp. 82–84, from the Thom pushforward and Euler self-intersection discussion through equations (4.2)–(4.4). It supplies a book treatment of Gysin, fixed-component reconstruction, and pushforward, while invoking Atiyah–Bott localization as input; it does not replace the local Borel-localization proof.
+
+## Assigned carriers and conventions
+
+- `def-abbv-equivariant-integration-conventions` (level 3) defines real Borel cohomology using the current batch-7 product Milnor model and period-one classes, character class `u_chi`, localization set, degree-shifting fiber integration, fiber-normalized Thom/Euler convention, and fixed-component orientation. It explicitly fixes `c1(L)=e(L_R)`, so the character classes used by the current Borel-localization statement generate exactly the same multiplicative set. It makes no Borel–Cartan comparison claim. Direct in-run supplier: `def-torus-equivariant-cohomology-cartan-model`; also assumes published `def-axiom-of-choice`. Exact carrier: `items/def-abbv-equivariant-integration-conventions.md`.
+- `lem-abbv-equivariant-thom-gysin-identities` (level 4) proves the Borel normal bundle is oriented and numerable, obtains its Thom class and isomorphism from published `thm-thom-isomorphism-for-oriented-vector-bundles`, defines the Gysin map by tubular excision, and proves self-intersection, disjoint-support restriction, and fiber integration. Its direct batch-8 base-property supplier `lem-qftx-borel-base-is-paracompact-of-cw-type` is now manifest-placed and its statement/proof interface matches; its current Step 1 record is missing, so the Gysin item remains escalated and the proof uses the base property conditionally. It also uses the selected Milnor numerability theorem and real Borel convention. Exact carrier: `items/lem-abbv-equivariant-thom-gysin-identities.md`.
+- `lem-abbv-fixed-component-euler-invertibility` (level 5) proves the fixed-locus tangent identity, absence of trivial normal weights, and normal Euler invertibility by the nonzero character product and finite geometric-series inverse. The invariant complex structure uses the period-one weight equation `chi(exp(sX))=exp(2π i s omega_chi(X))` and the normalized operator `A_X/(2π omega_chi(X))`. Rank-zero uses the empty product 1; the empty fixed locus is vacuous. Exact carrier: `items/lem-abbv-fixed-component-euler-invertibility.md`.
+- `thm-atiyah-bott-berline-vergne-integration-formula` (level 6) proves the compact fixed-component formula and its isolated-point specialization conditionally on the exact current Borel-localization statement. It extends the Gysin identities to the localized modules, handles empty fixed locus, rank-zero normals, and dimension zero, and retains the design boundary against direct claims for noncompact instanton spaces or infinite-dimensional field spaces. Its `[L2]` fact records the placed supplier statement and its missing current readiness records. Exact carrier: `items/thm-atiyah-bott-berline-vergne-integration-formula.md`.
+- `ex-abbv-projective-line-standard-circle-action` (level 7) computes the standard `S1` action on complex-oriented `CP1`: tangent weights `+1,-1`, dual-tautological restrictions `0,-u`, and sum `0/u+(-u)/(-u)=1`; a transverse section independently verifies the ordinary Euler number.
+- `ex-abbv-positive-dimensional-fixed-components` (level 7) computes `CP1 × CP1` with two fixed components: contributions 0 and 1, matching the product integral 1. Swapping the two real 2-plane orientations has sign `(-1)^(2·2)=+1`. Each example depends on the convention and conditional ABBV theorem; neither supplies the other.
+
+The assigned A/B page files are frontmatter-only with empty Markdown bodies. The A page lists the four A carriers; the B page lists both examples. No narrative page summaries were created.
+
+## Current cross-batch edges
+
+The required JSON array is maintained in `batch-9.cross-batch-dependencies.json`, one row per direct cross-batch edge:
+
+- verified interface edge: `def-abbv-equivariant-integration-conventions` → `def-torus-equivariant-cohomology-cartan-model`; current batch-7 statement, proof interface, manifest placement, and readiness record were inspected.
+- open edge: `lem-abbv-equivariant-thom-gysin-identities` → `lem-qftx-borel-base-is-paracompact-of-cw-type`; statement, proof, hypotheses, and manifest placement match the use, but this base-property item and its transitive compact-manifold cohomology supplier lack current Step 1 records.
+- open edge: `thm-atiyah-bott-berline-vergne-integration-formula` → `thm-borel-localization-for-compact-torus-actions`; exact statement, proof, and manifest placement match the conditional use, but the theorem and direct character-localization/base-property suppliers lack current Step 1 records.
+- verified page edge: `qftx-abbv-integration` → `qftx-borel-localization`; current page frontmatter and manifest inventory are populated and agree.
+
+Transitive observations about the character-localization item's stale claim that the batch-7 Borel definition lacks readiness, and the missing current Step 1 records for its consumers, are recorded here rather than as extra cross-batch review rows.
+
+## Final checks and Step 1 dispositions
+
+Current authoring edits include the six carriers, the two A/B page files, batch-9 manifest, proof contracts, coverage, notes, and cross-batch dependency array. Final strict proof-contract, dependency-level, content-policy, dependency-closure, render, source-fetch, and `proof-layout` results are to be appended here after the last edits. Record local convention readiness as ready only after those checks; record Gysin and its consumers escalated while their required batch-8 Step 1 records/proof inputs remain unresolved. Do not overwrite an existing escalation or mark a downstream item ready through an unresolved input.

